From bed4e1850afb64172b152fbbfe44cba6c9799713 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 19:04:24 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] flashnext cuda: --precision checkpoint runs routed NVFP4
 experts on NVFP4 rows

A ModelOpt NVFP4 pack states an input scale beside each routed expert
projection's weight scales: the quantizer calibrated NVFP4 activations.
The default keeps bf16 rows against FP4 weights decoded in registers.
--precision checkpoint takes the pack's own math on Blackwell: the
layer's rows to NVFP4 once (tf_ck_quant4), gate and up on the FP4 mma
into NVFP4 pair rows (tf_ck4_swiglu_nvfp4), down on the FP4 mma into the
fp32 slot rows (tf_ck4_down_f32_skip), with decode, few-row and prompt
tiles of one arithmetic so a row's bits do not depend on its pass.

It changes tokens, so it is opt-in: --precision full, the default,
loads and runs as before. One rank only, sm_120 and sm_121 only; a pack
without input scales is refused by name. Disk states key on the mode.
The tiles are registered with the kernel contract against an fp64
reference, and flashnext-kl compares the two modes' logits.
